  "diagnosis": {
    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 5.2,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.97,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings level off at about 1.1 from 6 h onward. That flat line is typical of a plate reader hitting its upper limit, not necessarily of growth stopping. I diluted the retained 18 h aliquot and re-read it. At 10x it read 0.5275 and 0.5177 (mean 0.523, so about 5.23 in undiluted terms). At 20x it read 0.2601 and 0.2575 (mean 0.259, so about 5.18). The two dilutions agree to within about 1%, so diluted readings are proportional to concentration. The true OD at 18 h is about 5.2, roughly 4.7 times the undiluted reading of 1.10. The 15 h aliquot (0.5257 at 10x, about 5.26) and the 12 h aliquot (0.5249 at 10x, about 5.25) give the same value. So the culture appears to sit at a true plateau of about 5.2 through the final hours, well above what the undiluted readings show. These two are single reads at a single dilution, so they rest on the proportionality shown at 18 h. The flat undiluted values from about 6 h onward reflect the reader's upper limit (about 1.1), not the true biomass. Because I didn't dilute any aliquot from before 12 h, I can't tell when growth actually reached its plateau."
  },
